From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH local 005] panvk: report "Panvk" / "Mesa 26.3.0-devel" as the driver identity

DXVK HUD and DXVKHUB read VK_KHR_driver_properties. Until now driverName
was the lower-case "panvk" and driverInfo was "PanVK-kbase beta.18-rc2
(Mesa 26.3.0-devel (git-...))" from csf-v11/099, which the tools show as
the driver name/version.

Report the short name "Panvk" and the plain release string
"Mesa 26.3.0-devel" so DXVK/DXVKHUB show the driver and version the way
the release is named. The PanVK-kbase release tag stays available in the
logs (csf-v11/118 prints driverName/deviceName/driverInfo at INFO).

Purpose: fix the driver name/version shown by DXVK HUD and DXVKHUB.
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (build), no behaviour change on the GPU.
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21.
Mesa base range: 26.3.0-devel (pinned 5a07217f), patches through local/004.
Dependencies: none (must come after csf-v11/099, which it rewrites).
Validation test: `strings libvulkan_panfrost.so | grep 'Mesa 26.3.0-devel'`
and the INFO startup line "Panvk (<gpu>) Mesa 26.3.0-devel".

Generated-by: LLM

--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c
@@ -1450,10 +1450,11 @@
    STATIC_ASSERT(sizeof(instance->driver_build_sha) >= VK_UUID_SIZE);
    memcpy(properties->driverUUID, instance->driver_build_sha, VK_UUID_SIZE);
 
-   snprintf(properties->driverName, VK_MAX_DRIVER_NAME_SIZE, "panvk");
+   /* Identity shown by DXVK HUD / DXVKHUB: the driver is presented as
+    * "Panvk", the version as the plain Mesa release. */
+   snprintf(properties->driverName, VK_MAX_DRIVER_NAME_SIZE, "Panvk");
    snprintf(properties->driverInfo, VK_MAX_DRIVER_INFO_SIZE,
-            "PanVK-kbase " PANVK_KBASE_RELEASE " (Mesa " PACKAGE_VERSION
-            MESA_GIT_SHA1 ")");
+            "Mesa " PACKAGE_VERSION);
 
    /* VK_EXT_physical_device_drm */
    if (device->drm.primary_rdev) {
